 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Most road tyres need an air top up every couple of months. Look at the sidewall for a figure like five to twelve, and check the pressure every week or two. Most tyres say the pressure on the sidewall, usually in PSI, which means pounds per square inch. That's not ideal. A proper pump with a gauge tells you exactly what you' at. Usually lower. Wet roads are slippery, and a tyre that's too high will bounce and wear out faster.",
